class Solution:
    def leaders(self, nums):
        n = len(nums)
        res = []
        current = nums[n - 1]

        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
            if nums[i] >= current:
                res.append(nums[i])
                current = nums[i]

        return res[::-1]

Logic:
Start from the rightmost element.
Keep track of the maximum seen so far (current).
If the current element is greater than or equal to current, it's a leader.
Update current.
Reverse the result at the end.
🧠 Memory Trick

"Right Max becomes the Leader."

⏱️ Complexity
Time: O(n) (single traversal + reverse)
Space: O(n) (to store the leaders)
🔥 One-Line Formula

"Traverse from right → Compare with right maximum → Update → Reverse."
